he hardest months you have faced. That takes discipline, courage, and a level of self-care that many people never develop. You did it not because it was easy but because you understand that your health matters, that you matter, even when everything else is demanding your attention."},{"id":"s6","title":"Look ahead with confidence","body":"The month is over. You survived it. Now look forward. The next month might be easier, or it might not. But you have proven to yourself that you can maintain your commitment to your health even under pressure. That knowledge is powerful. It means that no matter what comes next, you have evidence that you can handle it.\\n\\nIf this month drained your resources, take practical steps to rebuild. Check your Jireh Care Saver balance and set a small weekly contribution toward next month''s medication. If you fell behind on a health metric, schedule a check-up to get back on track. If you isolated yourself emotionally during the crisis, reach out to someone in your Jireh Circle or a trusted friend and let them know how you are doing.\\n\\nYou showed up when it was hardest. On easy days, anyone can follow a health plan. On hard days, only the committed do. You are committed. Give yourself the credit you have earned."}]'::jsonb, 7, '{"Recognise and celebrate the progress you have made","Understand what this milestone means for your health","Set meaningful goals for the next phase of your journey"}', E'progress-chart')
